WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.880
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:14.160
Today we will see how and what DeepMind's AI is&nbsp;
able to learn from a human, but with a twist!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:21.280
And the twist is that we are going to remove the&nbsp;
human teacher from the game, and see what happens.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:28.720
Is it just memorizing what the human does,&nbsp;
or is this AI capable of independent thought?

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:36.080
Their previous technique did something like&nbsp;
that, like guiding us to the bathroom, start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:44.320
a band together, or even find out the limitations&nbsp;
of the physics within this virtual world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:50.320
However, there is a big difference. This&nbsp;
previous technique had time to study.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.480
This one, not so much! This new one&nbsp;
has to do the learning on the job.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:04.080
Oh yes, in this project, we will see an&nbsp;
AI that has no pre-collected human data.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:11.600
It really has to learn everything on the&nbsp;
job. So, can it? Well, let's see together!

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:18.480
Phase 1 - Pandemonium. Here, the&nbsp;
AI says, well, here we do…things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:29.280
I am not so sure. Occasionally, it gets a point,&nbsp;
but now, look, uh-oh! The red teacher is gone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:37.680
And…oh boy, it gets very confused. It does&nbsp;
not have much of an idea what is going on.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:45.760
But, a bit of learning happens, and later.&nbsp;
Phase 2 - Following. It is still still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.080
not sure what is going on, but&nbsp;
when it follows this red chap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:57.200
it realized that it is getting a much&nbsp;
higher score. Before, it only got 2, now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:04.560
look at it! It is learning something new&nbsp;
here. And, look! He is gone again, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:13.040
it knows what to do. Well, kind of. It still&nbsp;
probably wonders, why its score is decreasing?

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:22.160
So, a bit later, Phase 3 - Memorization. First,&nbsp;
the usual dance with the demonstrator. But, now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:28.160
when he is gone, it knows exactly what to&nbsp;
do, and just keeps improving its score.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:36.000
And then comes the crown jewel. Phase&nbsp;
4 - Independence. No demonstrator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.640
anywhere to be seen. This is the final&nbsp;
exam. It has to be able to independently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:49.840
solve the problem. But here comes the twist.&nbsp;
For the previous phase, we said memorization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:57.840
and for this, we say independence. Why is this&nbsp;
different? Well, look. Do you see the difference?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:05.280
Hold on to your papers, because we have switched&nbsp;
up the colors. So, the previous strategy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:13.840
is suddenly useless. Oh yes! If it walks the same&nbsp;
path as before, it will not get a good score,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:21.520
and initially, that's what it is trying to&nbsp;
do. But, over time, it is now able to learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:26.800
independently, and indeed, find&nbsp;
the correct order by itself.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:35.840
And, what I absolutely loved here is, look.&nbsp;
Over time, the charts verify that indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:41.680
as soon as we take away the teacher, it&nbsp;
starts using different neurons as right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:48.320
after becoming an independent entity.&nbsp;
I love it. What an incredible chart.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:54.480
And all this is excellent news. So, if&nbsp;
it really has an intelligence of sorts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.000
it has to be able to deal with&nbsp;
previously unseen conditions and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.720
problems. That sounds super fun&nbsp;
- let’s explore that some more.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:13.840
Let’s give it a horizontal obstacle.&nbsp;
Good! Not a problem. Vertical?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:25.440
Also fine. Now, let’s make the world larger! And,&nbsp;
it is still doing well. Awesome! So, I absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:31.840
love this paper. DeepMind demonstrated that&nbsp;
they can build an AI that learns on the job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.080
one that is even capable of independent thought,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:43.200
and even better, one that can deal with unforeseen&nbsp;
situations too. What a time to be alive!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.920
So, what do you think? What&nbsp;
else could this be useful for?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.600
What do you expect to happen a&nbsp;
couple more papers down the line?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.840
Please let me know in the comments&nbsp;
below. I’d love to hear your thoughts.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.000
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

